Spec: LibResolvService

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Resolve published service records — the entries of `context.cluster.services` and
    `context.tenant.services` that other `ServiceInstance`/`TenantInstance` CRs publish — by
    exact service `key` or by publishing package name (exact or glob), and inline their cluster
    payload: a resolved record whose `definition` points at a ConfigMap (a Secret via
    @resolv_secret) comes back with that object's `data` folded into the returned map, so a
    package script gets one plain connection+config value for cross-service wiring. The file
    itself never computes a host/port/url: connection fields arrive already flattened by the
    context producers it consumes.

Exposes:
  All fourteen in-file `@fn` declarations are the module surface, reached as
    `svc::name(...)` under the `import "resolv_service" as svc` convention of the only
    in-repo importer, @/agent/tests/rhai_lib.rs; nothing runs at import time (pure declarations).
  @resolv_cm(svc) — enrich-one: when `svc?.definition?.kind == "ConfigMap"` pull that ConfigMap
    and merge its `data` over the record, then drop `definition`; otherwise return the record
    untouched. Every hit of every lookup below passes through it.
  @resolv_secret(svc) — the Secret twin: same guard/drop posture, values merged are
    @base64_decode of each `.data` key; not called by any function in this file.
  @get_from_key(svcs, names) — first array record whose `key` equals a wanted name.
  @get_from_package(svcs, names) / @get_from_package(svcs, key, names) — arity overloads: first
    record whose `"package".name` equals a wanted name, the 3-arg form conjoined with `s.key == key`.
  @service_glob(svcs, matcher) — all records with `@glob(s["package"].name, matcher)`,
    @resolv_cm-mapped, returned as an array.
  @get_system(context, names) / @get_tenant(context, names) — @get_from_key over
    `context?.cluster?.services` / `context?.tenant?.services`.
  @get_system_package(context, names) / (context, key, names) and @get_tenant_package(context,
    names) / (context, key, names) — same lane split over @get_from_package, both arities.
  @glob_system_package(context, pattern) / @glob_tenant_package(context, pattern) — @service_glob
    over the two context lanes.

Accepts:
  Records — array elements must be maps as the producers mint them (see `Depends on`): `key`
    (String), `"package"` (map with `name`), `definition` (@Children shape: `kind`, `name`,
    `namespace`), plus passthrough fields (`fqdn`, `port`, `instance`, `tenant`) which this file
    reads never and forwards verbatim. Records missing `key` are simply non-matches for the key
    lanes (missing map property answers `()`); records missing `"package"` are not tolerated by
    the package/glob lanes (see `Raises`).
  @svcs — the record array, or `()` (the guard), anything else is unguarded (see `Raises`).
  @names — @String matched by full equality, or an iterable treated as a preference list: the
    first name in @names order that matches anything wins; other types raise in the `for`.
  @matcher — glob pattern text for the engine @glob helper (wildmatch semantics).
  @context — the run-context map; safe-nav `?.` chains make an absent lane answer `()` instead
    of raising, so tenant-lane functions on a service-instance context and cluster-lane
    functions without `build_context` output both degrade to "not found".

Returns:
  Lookup hits — one record map (or an array of them in @service_glob), never an aggregate of
    multiple matches, never wrapped. Lookup misses — `()`, always: no @throw exists anywhere in
    the file and absence never raises. Merged maps keep every original record key not overwritten
    by the fetched `data` plus/minus what `Must` lists.
  @resolv_cm / @resolv_secret return the (possibly enriched) record itself — including for a
    `()` or `definition`-free input.

Raises:
  No @throw and no typed error: the only uncaught interpreter errors are rhai shape failures —
    a record whose `"package"` index answers `()` (or a non-map) followed by `.name` on it, in
    @get_from_package (both arities; the 3-arg form only for records already matching `key`) and
    in @service_glob (every record, it is the predicate), and @filter not existing on a
    non-array @svcs. No `?.` guards protect these indexes; the caller sees the raw interpreter error.
  Every @k8s_resource failure inside the two enrichers is caught and logged, never raised (@rhai_err
    turns engine errors into string-carrying texts, so the catch's `type_of(e) == "string"`
    branch takes them to @log_warn; other thrown values go to @log_warn(@json_encode(e))).

Handles:
  `svcs == ()` — the first statement of every lookup returns `()` unchanged.
  Non-ConfigMap / `definition`-free records — returned as-is, `definition` key kept (the
    `@remove("definition")` sits inside the kind branch).
  ConfigMap fetch failure (kind/CRD unresolved, object absent, no `.data`, bad namespace
    coordinate) — @log_warn, no data merged, but `definition` is still dropped, and the record
    is returned, not replaced by `()`.
  Secret decode failure on some mid-loop key — earlier keys stay decoded into the record
    (partial merge), then @log_warn and the `definition` drop.
  Array @names with no match, and any non-hit path — the trailing `()`.

Must:
  Read only four record fields: `key`, `"package".name`, and `definition.kind` / `definition.name`
    / `definition.namespace`; the enrichers touch no other cluster kind beyond the literal
    @k8s_resource("ConfigMap", ns) / @k8s_resource("Secret", ns) `@get(name)` lookup — no
    typed-instance getter (`get_instance` family) is imported.
  Take the first element of the filtered array (`found[0]`, @svcs order) as the one match; array
    @names resolve by caller-preference order, first name with any match wins.
  Merge fetched `data` over the record with `+=` (or per-key assignment for Secrets): colliding
    data keys overwrite record keys such as `key`/`fqdn`/`port`, and Secret values are stored
    decoded via @base64_decode, never as base64 text.
  Drop `definition` from enriched records on both the success and the swallowed-failure leg of
    each kind branch, and keep it on every other record.
  Stay mutation-free toward the caller: enrichment happens on a by-value copy (rai
    clone-on-write parameter semantics), so the @svcs/@context maps the caller owns never gain
    data or lose `definition`.
  Freeze the `?.` posture: enrichers and context wrappers safe-navigate, lookup predicates do
    not — which is exactly why `"package"`-free records raise while `key`-free ones miss.
  Keep the 2-arg/3-arg overloads of @get_from_package, @get_system_package and @get_tenant_package
    coexisting as distinct signatures (rhai dispatches by arity).

Depends on:
  wynil-core `0.7.7` engine API — @k8s_resource(kind, ns)`@get` on the `K8sGeneric` lane of
    @k8sgeneric_rhai_register, @glob (./glob.rs-style `glob(text, pattern)` helper), @log_warn,
    @json_encode, @base64_decode: the string-error conversion is @rhai_err / @error_chain; host
    ownership behind the @/common/src/rhaihandler.sdd assembly.
  Record shape producers (read context, not owned here): @/agent/scripts/lib/build_context.sdd —
    `cluster.services` entries with `fqdn`/`port` already flattened, `"package"` and `instance`
    attached, `definition` verbatim; `../tenant/context.rhai` — the `tenant.services` twin
    (`tenant:`-filtered only in the cluster lane; this file applies no `tenant` filtering itself).
  @/common/src/instanceservice.sdd + @/common/src/lib.sdd — the `ServiceInstance` CR whose
    `status.services` (@Published with `@Children` `definition`) the producers enumerate: the
    upstream source of every key this library matches.
  @rhai `?.`-returns-`()` on unit/missing properties, map index miss answering `()`, map `+=`
    merge, `@remove` on maps, and @filter/@map/@len array helpers.

References:
  @/agent/tests/rhai_lib.rs — sole importer to date (`make_lib_script`, resolver dir
    `./scripts/lib`, mock engine with empty k8s mocks); five tests pin the pure-map lanes only.
  `/docs/packages/lifecycle.md` — advertises this library to package authors as the
    service-discovery toolkit lane.

Scenario: key hit inlines ConfigMap data
  Given a cluster-lane record `#{key: "pg", fqdn: "pg.ns", port: 5432, definition: #{kind: "ConfigMap", name: "pg-conf", namespace: "ns"}}`
  When @get_from_key(svcs, "pg") runs and the ConfigMap fetch answers `#{data: #{tls: "on"}}`
  Then the return carries `key`/`fqdn`/`port` 5432 plus `tls: "on"`, and no longer contains `definition`

Scenario: key miss answers unit, never an error
  Given the same @svcs
  When @get_from_key(svcs, "nonexistent") runs
  Then the result is `()` with no cluster call and no throw
  Maps to @resolv_service_get_from_key_returns_unit_when_not_found (and the hit half to
    @resolv_service_get_from_key_finds_service — those fixtures carry no `definition`, so the
    enricher runs as a typed no-op there)

Scenario: array names keep caller order authoritative
  Given records listed secondary-first
  When @get_from_key(svcs, ["primary", "secondary"]) runs
  Then the `primary` record returns, though `secondary` stands first in @svcs
  Maps to @resolv_service_get_from_key_with_array_of_names

Scenario: package-name lanes, exact and paired
  Given records each carrying `"package"` `#{name: ...}`
  When @get_from_package(svcs, "postgresql") runs, then @get_from_package(svcs, "svc1", "redis")
  Then the first returns the `svc1` record, the second the record whose `key` and package name
    both match, and a name no record publishes answers `()`
  Maps to @resolv_service_get_from_package_finds_by_package_name (2-arg leg only)

Scenario: glob lanes return every match or unit
  Given three records, two carrying package names `postgres-*` matches
  When @service_glob(svcs, "postgres-*") runs
  Then an array of the two @resolv_cm-mapped records returns; a pattern matching nothing answers
    `()` — not an empty array
  Maps to @resolv_service_service_glob_filters_and_maps (miss leg unmapped)

Scenario: ConfigMap lookup failure is swallowed but shaping continues
  Given a `ConfigMap`-kinded record whose object no longer exists
  When any lookup resolves it
  Then @log_warn carries the fetch text, no data appears in the result, yet the record returns
    minus `definition`
  No mapped test exists; see the open task below.

Scenario: Secret records pass through lookups, decode only via @resolv_secret
  Given a record with `definition.kind: "Secret"`
  When @get_from_key resolves it
  Then it returns exactly as stored, `definition` intact — no lookup lane auto-resolves Secrets
  But @resolv_secret(svc) on the same record returns it with each `.data` key base64-decoded and
    `definition` removed
  No mapped test exists for either leg.

Scenario: malformed records raise in the package lanes only
  Given an @svcs array in which one record carries no `"package"` key
  When @get_from_package or @service_glob filters it
  Then the whole call dies on the interpreter property-access error, uncaught
  But @get_from_key over the same array returns normally
  No mapped test exists; see the open task below.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover the cluster lane with @make_lib_script_with_k8s: the ConfigMap hit, miss-swallow and
      Secret-decode scenarios above, plus the package-lane raise and the glob miss leg — the five
      current tests never set `definition`, so no fetch branch executes today.
  [?] Freeze the tier: no shipped script imports this library (repo grep finds only the test
      file); decide later whether it is the public service-discovery surface for boxes/packages
      or a dormant toolkit, and whether @resolv_secret — called from nothing — stays exposed.
  [?] Decide return shapes: @service_glob answers `()`-or-array while every multi-match lookup
      silently truncates to the first match; unify to always-list or document the truncation.
  [?] Merge precedence: fetched data keys overwrite the record's own `key`/`fqdn`/`port`; decide
      whether connection fields must win instead.
  [?] @resolv_secret partial merge: the loop leaves earlier decoded keys in place when a later
      @base64_decode throws; decide whether to prevalidate or roll back.
  [?] Findings left unfixed: the `s["package"].name` predicates carry no `?.` so one malformed
      record aborts a whole lookup, @service_glob ends in an unreachable trailing `()` after both
      branches already return, and `get_tenant_package(context, names)` reads `tenant.services`
      entries that only TenantInstance contexts carry — confirm each posture or correct it.

Done when:
  Every scenario above has a mapped test (mock-k8s lane included), the tier and shape decisions
    are recorded, and `cargo test -p agent` is green.
